          "id": "india-fertiliser-subsidy-rabi-2026-11-11",
          "headline": "Cabinet approves Rs 62,370 crore fertiliser subsidy for the rabi season",
          "summary": "The Union Cabinet set nutrient-based subsidy rates on phosphatic and potassic fertilisers, including DAP, for October 2026 to March 2027. The bill is about Rs 62,370 crore, roughly Rs 24,418 crore more than last rabi season's Rs 37,952 crore. Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw linked it to higher world prices of fertilisers and inputs such as sulphur.",
